dpsp-fundamental-duties.synthesis:
- **Recurring concepts:** welfare state; socio-economic democracy; Article 37; Gandhian DPSPs; article-content mapping; 42nd Amendment additions; complete FD list; environment overlap.
- **Recurring traps:**
  - non-justiciable ≠ constitutionally unimportant;
  - “fundamental in governance” ≠ judicially enforceable;
  - DPSPs guide legislative/executive action ≠ limitations on their functions;
  - vote ≠ Fundamental Duty;
  - monuments ≠ Fundamental Duty;
  - environment = **both** DPSP + FD.
- **Qualifier patterns:** *not*, *both*, *which Part*, *fundamental*, *enforceable*, *added by*, *correctly matched*.
- **UPSC vs UPPCS:** UPSC → conceptual qualifiers + elimination; UPPCS → denser article/Part/amendment/source recall.
- **Recent reinforcement:** UPPCS 2022–2025 repeatedly tests Part/article mapping, DPSP–FD overlap and assertion/matching formats; last direct UPSC canonical reinforcement in this node is 2021.
